THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
SRC_003 adds a committed-root checkpoint that suspends any root whose only defenders are UNDEC before it is committed. But in the grounded extension, a node that is attacked but unattacked-and-undefended remains UNDEC, so an unattacked root with no committed defenders would be held suspended under this rule, even though the grounded extension accepts it — breaking the existing guarantee that every committed root is valid and altering the fixpoint's content despite the claim it does not alter it.

TARGET:
Add a committed-root checkpoint that does not alter the fixpoint: before any root is committed, verify the set of committed roots is conflict-free and every committed root is defended by already-committed roots; any root whose only defenders are UNDEC is held suspended. Determinism and polynomial cost are untouched since this is a post-check on a subset of nodes, and committed-root validity becomes an explicit, machine-checkable invariant rather than an implicit property.